[low] [scripts/tests/test_commission_manifest.sh:878](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/fix-tc79/scripts/tests/test_commission_manifest.sh:878) depends on the literal warning glyph plus `HISTORICAL`. If `commission-manifest.sh` keeps the semantic banner but changes presentation to ASCII, e.g. `WARNING HISTORICAL`, this arm fails even though the behavior is intact. Matching `HISTORICAL` plus the slice-specific text would make it less formatting-sensitive.

**No [P1] findings.** I don’t see a vacuous green path in the new arm: unreadable/malformed state, `next_slice: null`, no predecessor, missing predecessor SHA, failed generator run, missing base line, wrong SHA, wrong slice label, and banner mismatch all route to `fail`. The `set +e` regions capture and check return codes, and the `read ... || true` does not create a silent pass because `${D9D_OK:-}` must be `OK`.

**No [P2] findings.** The arm does use the same state file as the tool for expected target/base/banner state, so it cannot catch defects where the state file itself is wrong or internally inconsistent but both derivations interpret it the same way. It can catch generator drift from that state-derived contract: wrong predecessor selection, wrong base-line SHA, wrong slice label, generator failure, or banner presence not matching `target in landed`. In the current state, `next_slice` is Slice 30 and pending, so this real-repo arm exercises the “banner absent” side; the “banner present for landed target” side remains covered by fixture arm 8f, not by this real-state arm.

Verified with `bash scripts/tests/test_commission_manifest.sh`; it passes.
